3.3  COPYRIGHT MANAGEMENT INFORMATION. The license identifier, copyright
     header, author statement, TK Label notices, and the source-file header
     block set out in Annex C constitute "copyright management information"
     (CMI) within the meaning of 17 U.S.C. § 1202(c), because they identify
     the work, its author, its copyright owner, and the terms and conditions
     for use of the work, and are conveyed in connection with copies of the
     Work. Removal or alteration of CMI, or distribution of the Work knowing
     CMI has been removed or altered, violates 17 U.S.C. § 1202(b) and is a
     condition-breach under Section 2.2. The Licensor notes that courts
     currently require a showing of knowledge and reasonable grounds to know
     that removal will facilitate infringement (e.g., Raw Story Media v.
     OpenAI (S.D.N.Y. 2024)); Licensees are therefore placed on actual notice
     by this Section that removal or alteration of CMI facilitates
     infringement of this License.

3.4  NO FALSE DESIGNATION. No Licensee may use the Work in any manner
     likely to cause confusion as to the Work's Indigenous origin, tribal
     affiliation, or sponsorship, including in commerce. This condition
     supports, and does not limit, remedies under Section 43(a) of the
     Lanham Act, 15 U.S.C. § 1125(a).

3.5  REGISTRATION NOTICE. The Licensor maintains or will maintain timely
     copyright registrations of the Work to preserve eligibility for
     statutory damages and attorney's fees under 17 U.S.C. §§ 411(a) and 412.
     Licensees should assume all components of the Work are registered.

