15. GOVERNING LAW AND INTERNATIONAL INSTRUMENTS
============================================================================

15.1 LAYERED GOVERNING LAW. This License is governed, in descending order
     of primacy as each applies by its own force, by: (a) federal law of the
     United States, including copyright law and federal Indian law; (b) the
     Constitution, statutes, and common law of the Grand Traverse Band of
     Ottawa and Chippewa Indians as to Community Protocols and consensual
     tribal-jurisdiction matters; (c) Community Protocols (Annex B); (d) the
     laws of the State of Michigan solely to the extent not in conflict with
     (a)-(c); and (e) the Indigenous-rights norms of the instruments in
     Annex A as interpretive authorities and rules of construction, each to
     the precise extent of its legal status as stated there (binding treaty,
     endorsed declaration, signed-unratified, or persuasive).

15.2 INTERNATIONAL INCORPORATION TABLE. Annex A lists each cited
     international instrument, its adoption date, its status for the United
     States (party, signed-not-ratified, endorsed, non-party/persuasive), and
     the sections of this License each supports. No instrument is claimed to
     have force it does not have; several — including WIPO GRATK Art. 3 and
     UNDRIP Arts. 11, 31, 37, and 40 — are adopted here as contractual
     commitments binding the parties even where the instruments are not
     self-executing or the United States is not a party.

15.3 AMERICAN DECLARATION. The American Declaration on the Rights of
     Indigenous Peoples (adopted by the OAS General Assembly, June 15, 2016)
     supports this License's cultural-heritage and intellectual-property
     positions as interpretive authority within the inter-American system.

============================================================================
16. IDENTITY OF RIGHTS; NO WAIVER; IMMUNITY RESERVED
============================================================================

16.1 INDIVIDUAL LICENSOR, COMMUNAL DIMENSIONS. The Licensor is an
     individual member of a tribal nation. He asserts: (a) his private
     property rights as author and copyright owner; (b) rights stewarded for
     the Community in TK, TCEs, and Cultural Patrimony that no individual can
     alienate (Section 8.1); and (c) treaty-informed cultural rights as a
     beneficiary of the Treaties.

16.2 NO PERSONAL CLAIM OF TRIBAL IMMUNITY. Tribal sovereign immunity
     belongs to tribal governments and their arms and officials acting in
     their official capacities (Michigan v. Bay Mills Indian Community, 572
     U.S. 782 (2014); Kiowa Tribe v. Manufacturing Technologies, 523 U.S. 751
     (1998)); an individual member acting privately does not personally hold
     that immunity, and this License does not claim otherwise. Conversely,
     nothing in this License, and no act of the Licensor, waives or diminishes
     the sovereign immunity of the GTB, the LTBB, or any other tribal
     government; and nothing herein purports to bind any tribal government.

16.3 STANDING TO ENFORCE; FUTURE TRIBAL RECOGNITION. This License is
     enforceable by the Licensor personally. If the GTB Tribal Council, an
     LTBB governmental body, or a duly constituted Beaver Island Band
     community authority adopts a resolution recognizing this License or the
     Community's interest in the Work, such recognition shall supplement —
     and never be required to support — the Licensor's private rights, and
     may add the enforcing community's governmental remedies where law
     permits.

16.4 NO WAIVER. No failure to enforce any provision is a waiver. No
     acceptance of performance is acquiescence in an unlicensed use.

============================================================================
17. SEVERABILITY AND THE ENFORCEMENT FALLBACK LADDER
============================================================================

17.1 BLUE-PENCIL RULE. If any provision of this License is held
     unenforceable, it shall be reformed to the maximum enforceable scope;
     if reformation is impossible, it is severed. Each maximal provision of
     this License is paired with a fallback rung (Sections 12.2, 13.3); the
     License is drafted to degrade gracefully, preserving the strongest
     enforceable protection at every level rather than risking total
     invalidation.

17.2 SURVIVAL. Sections 1-5, 8, 10, 12.3, 13, 14, 15, 16, and 17 survive
     termination or revocation to the extent needed to enforce accrued
     rights, deletion duties, and remedies.

